anies in the universe; the top four hold 40% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 45% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the top of its 52-week range, 7% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 25% and a beta of 0.52, it is more defensive than the market, though its beta has shifted (1y -0.68 vs 5y 0.40), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $1.7B traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 55% in the 2020 crash, 25% in the 2022 bear market and 44% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $144 (margin of safety -53%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 28%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $113 to $185 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Energy peers: P/FCF 25.9 vs 14.6 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 124% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.9% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 24 covering analysts target $242 on average, 10% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 10% earns above the cost of capital of 8.0%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.76).","It converts 9% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.76x.","ROE of 7% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.7x equity multiplier)."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 1.2x net debt to EBITDA ($12.8B of cash against $50.7B of debt), with interest covered 17.2x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -8.4% over 3 years, 14.8% over 5 years and 3.2% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 28%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 58.6% a year over five years.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 9.2% of sales), a maintenance pace.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 17.0% on average.","Analysts expect -9.5% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.8%, and institutions hold 72%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (20 sales, net $268.8M sold).","It returns 5.8% a year to shareholders (2.8% in buybacks and 3.2% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 42 consecutive years, raising it 5.7% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 43,039 employees, each generates about $4.4M of revenue, 2.2x the Energy median.","That works out to $386K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $7.8M (2x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":57,"head":"Avoid: priced 53% above its fair value of $144.","pros":["Revenue grew 14.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 1.2x","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +45%","Returns 5.8% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 53% above fair value of $144","P/FCF 25.9x vs sector 14.6x"],"flags":["Priced 53% above its fair value of $144"],"need":[],"buy_below":122.28,"vc":{"base":143.86,"base_src":"dcf","bear":113.34,"bull":185.26,"alt_median":86.0,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.7222,"dispersion":0.2824,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 72% above the other models' median ($86.00)"]},"med":{"pe":13.5876,"ev_ebitda":7.146,"pfcf":14.6331,"pb":1.7432,"roic":0.0952,"gross_margin":0.2462,"fcf_margin":0.0762,"div_yield":0.0357}},"mc_quantiles":[92.89,106.33,113.34,118.62,122.92,127.52,131.53,134.34,137.89,140.84,144.97,147.88,151.28,156.33,159.4,165.0,170.58,176.47,185.26,199.06,224.44],"mc_drivers":{"growth":0.488,"discount_rate":0.406,"terminal_growth":0.036,"exit_multiple":0.07},"ticker":"CVX","date":"2026-11-13"}